From: jaewun <jaewun@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] input: rsinput: suspend the gamepad MCU across system sleep

The gamepad MCU streams input reports continuously over the UART. Across a
system-suspend teardown the MCU keeps sending, so the geni-serial RX interrupt
storms while the port is stopping, the primary handler returns IRQ_NONE, and the
kernel's spurious-IRQ detector permanently disables the UART IRQ -- the gamepad
is then dead after resume until the IRQ is re-requested.

Extend the existing generic RSInput suspend callback to quiesce the MCU by
dropping its enable rail and asserting reset, mirroring rsinput_remove(). The
generic resume callback re-powers and re-initialises it.

Signed-off-by: jaewun <jaewun@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/input/joystick/rsinput.c
+++ b/drivers/input/joystick/rsinput.c
@@ -643,6 +643,22 @@ static int rsinput_suspend(struct device *dev)
     if (drv->rumble_work.func)
         cancel_work_sync(&drv->rumble_work);
 
+    /*
+     * The MCU streams gamepad reports continuously over the UART. If it keeps
+     * sending across the system-suspend teardown, the geni-serial RX interrupt
+     * storms while the port is being stopped, the primary handler returns
+     * IRQ_NONE, and the kernel's spurious-IRQ detector permanently disables the
+     * UART IRQ -- leaving the gamepad dead after resume until the IRQ is
+     * re-requested. Quiesce the MCU (drop its enable rail and hold it in reset,
+     * mirroring rsinput_remove) so the line goes silent before the UART
+     * suspends; rsinput_resume() re-powers and re-initialises it.
+     */
+    if (drv->enable_gpio)
+        gpiod_set_value_cansleep(drv->enable_gpio, 0);
+
+    if (drv->reset_gpio)
+        gpiod_set_value_cansleep(drv->reset_gpio, 0);
+
     return 0;
 }
 
